The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms showing the expression of co-stimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). BMDCs were incubated for two days with either 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) or a medium control (gray line). The results indicate that Nano-11 treatment led to a slight increase in CD40 expression but a significant upregulation of CD80 and CD86. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to activate dendritic cells, a critical step for initiating an adaptive immune response and supporting its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.